This solution uses a graph to represent the intervals and uses Depth First Search (DFS) to detect cycles between intervals. If a cycle is found, it means there is no direct path between two intervals. The graph is preprocessed using a DFS on the first query to detect cycles, and this information is used to answer subsequent queries in constant time.

